    "passage": "Kofi and Rita were choosing pictures from a book to copy for a display. Kofi chose a bright bird, and Rita chose a house covered in flowers. They passed a plain picture of a wooden bench without stopping. Later, Kofi looked for somewhere to put his bird in their shared drawing. Rita suggested a tree, but the page already had two large trees. They turned back through the book and came to the bench again. Kofi drew it between the trees and placed the bird on its back. Rita added a person sitting there, looking towards the house covered in flowers. The plain bench now joined the different parts of their picture. When the teacher asked which book picture had helped most, they looked at each other. Then both pointed to the page they had nearly skipped. Rita placed a bookmark there before returning the book.",
